# Your financial data. This is the important line in this file.
#
# data/ holds wallet.db -- every purchase, with dates, merchants and amounts --
# and fx_rates.csv, which is derived. Neither belongs in a repository, and the
# first one belongs in a public one least of all. If you add a feature that
# writes anything derived from a transaction, add it here in the same commit.
data/
*.db
*.csv

# ...except the sample, which is invented and is there so a clone has
# something to import.
!sample-statement.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Test artefacts
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# Editors
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
